# Do Not Connect to External Services

Never make live calls to, authenticate against, or modify configuration in any
third-party service this repo integrates with. This applies to development,
debugging, and verification alike.

## Services covered

Auth0 (`@auth0/auth0-angular`, tenant config, callback URLs, allowed origins),
OneSignal (`onesignal-ngx`, `OneSignalSDKWorker.js`, push registration), the
Nabarun backend APIs (`api_base_url`, `api_base_url2`), Google reCAPTCHA,
Google Analytics, and Firebase.

This list is not exhaustive. If something reaches the network and is not a
package registry, treat it as covered.

## What is not allowed

- Logging in, requesting tokens, or triggering an auth redirect to reach a page
- Registering for push notifications or hitting a OneSignal endpoint
- Calling backend endpoints, including to "just check" a response shape
- Editing tenant settings, allowed origins, callback URLs, API keys or secrets
- Adding real credentials to `src/environments/*.ts` or any committed file

## What to do instead

Verify at the build, type and DOM level: `ng build`, `tsc --noEmit`, unit tests,
and inspecting rendered markup on unauthenticated routes.

When a check genuinely requires a live service, stop and report it rather than
connecting. State plainly what could not be verified and hand it back as a
manual step.

```
❌ Log in through Auth0 to screenshot the dashboard route
✅ Confirm the route compiles and its guard redirects when unauthenticated,
   then list the authenticated routes as needing manual review
```

A 401, 403 or CORS error from one of these services during local work is
expected. Treat it as environment configuration, not a bug to fix by changing
the service.
